{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfgSTDG79vHDUzD3jqfQG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate, a refinement of the incumbent `person_pattern_sensitivity_rule_built`, and it passes the self-check. That check is only a short smoke fit, so it doesn't settle novelty, convergence or the 30-minute time limit; the short fit didn't finish clearly fast either.\n\n**Name:** `person_switch_ideal_pattern_rule_built`\n\n**The one change:** each person now has their own ideal switching rate, drawn from a population distribution, instead of one ideal shared by everyone. Everything else in the incumbent stays as it was: the tally-span judgement, the person-specific switching weight, the person-specific pattern sensitivity on chunk variety and the rule-built penalty, and the left/right lean.\n\n**Why this change:** the critique found that people differ in how often they agree with the majority even on pairs where pattern structure can't matter. On those pairs only tally span and switching are left. With a personal switching ideal, some people pick the more-switching sequence and others the less-switching one. That is the extra spread across people the incumbent couldn't produce. The critique's result was only raw-significant (p = 0.04) and did not survive the FDR correction (q = 0.32), so this is a weak lead.\n\n**Self-check result:**\n- It printed `OK`: the code loads, the log-probability is finite, the data contract holds, and ELPD-LOO is finite.\n- ELPD-LOO came out at −3263.6, against the incumbent's −3285.7. This comes from a 1-chain, 100-draw fit and is not a fair comparison with the incumbent's full fit.\n- PSIS-LOO was flagged unreliable: 13.7% of trials had a high Pareto k, against a 1% tolerance. That may be because the fit was so short, but I haven't confirmed it, so the ELPD figure above may also be off.\n- R-hat couldn't be computed from a single chain, so convergence wasn't checked.\n- The 200-iteration smoke fit took 223 seconds. Whether the full fit finishes in 30 minutes is unknown.\n\nThe three files are in the `candidate_3` directory: `hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt` and `candidate.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":72607,"cache_read_input_tokens":11602,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":72607,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74219054-c857-4622-9a85-839e8bbae939","uuid":"9d6f7399-268f-4f84-aed9-e644103f478d","timestamp":"2026-10-04T02:52:30.137Z","request_id":"req_011CfgSTCpp6ZJapjWzmTMcV"}
